# Ordinary project composition (PLAN-1095): modules, closures, tasks, CT and stdlib co-resident in one package

The canonical author of the ordinary-project composition family. Every case
carries ONE Auto source/project closure; the `av` check runs the ordinary AV
language chain (`ac-av/language-source-run-v1`). The four §6 draft cases land
here with the audited typed-lambda normalization (the face has no lambda
parameter inference — the frozen 1081/1082 rule, recorded in
`language/migration/legacy-map.tsv`).

## Case: module-closure-generic
id: "av.parity.1095.module-closure-generic"
tags: ["av-language-parity", "plan-1095", "composition"]
links: ["PLAN-1095"]
entry-mode: "program"

### Auto
path: "main.at"

```auto
use lib.id
fn twice(n int) int { return n * 2 }
fn main() int {
 let f = twice
 let xs = [id(19), id(23)]
 if f(xs[0]) + f(xs[1]) == 84 { return 42 }; return 0
}
```

#### lib.at

```auto
pub fn id<T>(x T) T { return x }
```

